<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>What Time Is It?</title>
  <page>
  <exercise workspace="2in">
          <introduction>
                  <p>
                          An (analog) clock has a minute hand that is <m>5\text{in}</m> long. We begin observing at noon. We also have a digital clock that is synced with the analog clock.
                  </p>
          </introduction>
          <task>
            <statement>
              <p>
                              What time is showing on the digital clock (including seconds) when the tip of the minute hand is first (after noon) <m>3\text{in}</m> horizontally to the left of the center of the clock? (That is, the tip of the minute hand is <m>3\text{in}</m> to the left of the line through the <m>12</m> and the <m>6</m> on the clock.)
              </p>
              <figure xml:id="fig_clock1">
                      <caption>Minute Hand Position on an Analog Clock</caption>
                      <image width="50%">
                              <description><p>An image of an analog clock. The minute hand has a length of five inches. The tip of the minute hand is 3 inches to the left of a line from the 12 to the 6 on the clock, between the 7 and 8 on the clock.</p></description>
                              <xi:include href="./clock1.xml"/>
                      </image>
              </figure>
            </statement>
          </task>
          <task>
                  <statement>
                          <p>
                              What time is showing on the digital clock (including seconds) when the tip of the minute hand is first (after noon) <m>2\text{in}</m> vertically below the center of the clock? (That is, the tip of the minute hand is <m>2\text{in}</m> below the line through the <m>9</m> and the <m>12</m> on the clock.)
                          </p>
                  </statement>
          </task>
  </exercise>
  </page>

</worksheet>
